The '''R1-series astromech droid''', also known as the '''R1 reactor drone''', was a model of [[R-series]] [[astromech droid]] manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]].

==Characteristics==
A part of the [[R-series]] of [[astromech droid]]s manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]], the R1-series astromech [[droid]],<ref name="New Edition" /> also known as the R1 [[reactor drone]],<ref name="Junior novelization">[[Star Wars: A New Hope (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: A New Hope'' junior novelization]]</ref> was tall compared to later R-units,<ref name="New Edition" /> standing 1.94 [[meter]]s in height.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> It moved slowly on a single [[Limb|foot]]<ref name="New Edition" /> and some,<ref name="Extraordinary Droids">''[[Star Wars: Extraordinary Droids]]''</ref> though not all,<ref name="A New Hope" /><ref name="The Blue Brothers">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=13|story=Tales from Wild Space: The Blue Brothers}}</ref> featured a long antenna atop their dome.<ref name="Extraordinary Droids" /> R1 units had a single [[Color|red]] [[photoreceptor]]<ref name="Chewie's Day Off" /> and [[Color|black]],<ref name="A New Hope" /> blue,<ref name="Chewie's Day Off" /> or gray plating.<ref name="A New Hope" /> They were so large that they could only be used on the biggest of [[starship]]s. R1 units were the first droids to be able to communicate in [[Binary|droidspeak]],<ref name="Extraordinary Droids" /> though they were far less personable than later R-units.<ref name="New Edition" /> They were equipped with a pair of [[Limb|arms]] tipped with manipulators<ref name="Gonk" /> and a [[holoprojector]].<ref name="Dark Lord of the Sith 14" />

==History==
The R1 unit was one of the oldest astromech models in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Extraordinary Droids" />

By the [[time]] of the [[Invasion of Naboo]], the [[Toydarian]] [[junk dealer]] [[Watto]] owned an R1 astromech, which was behind the counter in his [[Watto's junkshop|shop]]&mdash;situated in [[Mos Espa]] on the [[planet]] of [[Tatooine]]&mdash;when [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]], [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], and [[Gungan]] [[Jar Jar Binks]] entered the shop.<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> Said unit worked as a [[R1-type shopkeeping drone|shopkeeping drone]], handling most of Watto's daily business operations.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

Over thirty [[Standard year|years]] later, an R1 unit<ref name="A New Hope" /> designated [[R1-G4]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> fell into the hands of a group of diminutive [[Jawa]] [[scavenger]]s traveling in a [[sandcrawler]] on Tatooine. Those Jawas attempted to sell the astromech to the [[moisture farmer]] [[Owen Lars]] and his nephew [[Luke Skywalker]]. Lars, however, rejected the tall droid in favor of an [[R2-D2|R2 unit]] and [[C-3PO|3PO-series protocol droid]]&mdash;both of which were in fact [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] droids trying to carry out a [[Secret mission to Tatooine|secret mission]] at the behest of [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]]. Around the same time, two other R1 units were known to be present in the Tatooinian [[spaceport]] of [[Mos Eisley]].<ref name="A New Hope" />

[[File:New_Republic_Droid_Battles.png|thumb|right|150px|New Republic R1 security droids resembled a modified R1 units.]]
A modified R1 unit named "[[Bard]]" was the companion to the historian [[Tohan Lege]] and kept recordings of the many tales he had collected in his life, allowing him to posthumously participate in the [[Batuu]] festival known as the Fire of the Rising Moons.<ref name="Disneyland">{{Disney|subdomain=disneyland|domain=go.com|url=entertainment/disneyland/fire-of-the-rising-moons-fireworks|text=Disneyland: Fire of the Rising Moons}}</ref>

The [[New Republic]] made use of a similar looking droid series<ref name="Chapter 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref> known as the [[R1 security droid|R1 Security Droid]].<ref name="Droids Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|Assassin, Security, and Other Droids of War}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The R1-series astromech droid was originally created for the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="A New Hope" /> Set decorator [[Roger Christian]] designed the R1 unit that would later be identified as R1-G4 in homage to the art of illustrator [[Wikipedia:Chris Foss|Chris Foss]],<ref name="Roger Christian">{{WebCite|url=http://www.shadowlocked.com/20100309134/interviews/exclusive-interview-the-worlds-of-roger-christian.html#fossrobot|text=Exclusive interview: The worlds of Roger Christian|author=Anderson, Martin|date=2010-03-09|quote=In ''Star Wars'', there's a robot in the line-up with the sandcrawler when they're buying R2-D2 and C-3PO&hellipI did do a homage, because I felt I should, to Chris Foss, because he did some very early designs for that and he was always a favourite of mine. So I made one and designed it up out of scrap as if it might have been in a Chris Foss painting, and that was my homage to him, because I always thought he was a genius as an artist.|archivedate=20160406164204}}</ref> specifically a cover he had painted for a [[1973]] [[Wikipedia:Panther Books|Panther Science Fiction]] reprint of [[Wikipedia:Isaac Asimov|Isaac Asimov's]] [[1950s|1957]] novel ''[[Wikipedia:The Naked Sun|The Naked Sun]]''.<ref name="The Naked Sun">{{Amazon|url=Naked-Sun-Isaac-Asimov/dp/B002I4DI1Y|text=The Naked Sun}}</ref> The R1-G4 prop would be used to depict another R1 unit in Mos Eisley<ref name="A New Hope" /> and would become the basis for the R1-series astromech droid's appearance in most future sources.<ref name="Dark Lord of the Sith 14" /><ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref><ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref><ref name="Bounty Hunted">{{FOD|Bounty Hunted}}</ref><ref name="Droid Depot">{{GEAttr|text=Droid Depot}}</ref> A second R1 with a distinct design was also used in the film, appearing in the background when [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and Luke Skywalker are stopped and questioned by stormtroopers in Mos Eisley.<ref name="A New Hope" />

